{"author":"did:key:z6Mkmz8SWiUshwDMszSqwzMngt7ScNmsEj7vZoFRLjpcZTm9","evaluation":{"digest":{"sha256":"4152e3c052bab564dda76ad5ed1d03d6530a9c79fae2176c9d3e7d28f972c2d1"}},"instructions":"Return exactly ACCEPT or REJECT.","network.jinn.binary-judgment.item-sha256":"sha256:45459dc76683136477c7bcef1f8c5e14c5cb27de09e06b3f175cfc9498a85720","outputs":[{"mediaType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","name":"judge-response","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.jinn.binary-judgment.observation.v1+json","name":"judge-observation","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.inspect-ai.eval-log+json","name":"inspect-log","required":false}],"payload":{"candidateAnswer":"It reminds her of her mom.","evidence":"[D12:3 | 4:30 pm on 9 April, 2023] Deborah: My mom was interested in art. She believed art could give out strong emotions and uniquely connect us. When I go to an art show, it's like we're still experiencing it together even though she's gone. It's hard but comforting.","itemId":"urn:uuid:ef08cb5f-f470-58bd-b027-e0f26410b44e","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:450e91e73d3aa85293ea90919d2d6b875584b0897d632a16289d14ecad637750","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"What does Deborah find comforting about going to art shows?","referenceAnswer":"It makes her feel like she's still experiencing it with her mom","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"450e91e73d3aa85293ea90919d2d6b875584b0897d632a16289d14ecad637750"}}]},"profile":{"digest":{"sha256":"ebb34d8362e2cc3135847a5ad6f3ee3d9c2d9922a2b827aa9dfcbaf440b22557"},"uri":"https://spec.jinn.network/task-profiles/binary-judgment/2.0"},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/profiles/task-execution/v1"}